      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "ครับ and ค่ะ",
      "text": "Men end a polite sentence with ครับ; women end it with ค่ะ. Both also work as a polite \"yes\". There are no spaces between Thai words, so a word like ชื่อมะลิค่ะ is read as ชื่อ + มะลิ + ค่ะ.",
      "explains": [
        "th.polite-particle"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 0
    }
  ],
